{"id":"[REDACTED]","object":"chat.completion","created":1788222993,"model":"mercury-2","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"**NO_CONCRETE_BREAK_FOUND**\n\n*Evidence*\n\n1. **`scripts/generate-live-proof.js` loads `.env.gates`**  \n   ```js\n   require('dotenv').config({ path: path.join(__dirname, '..', '.env.gates') });\n   ```  \n   (lines 274‑276 of `scripts/generate-live‑proof.js`【open_file†L274-L276】)\n\n2. **The script decides the reported environment from `process.env.LIVE_TRADING`**  \n   ```js\n   env: process.env.LIVE_TRADING === 'true' ? 'LIVE' : 'PAPER',\n   ```  \n   (line 296 of `scripts/generate-live‑proof.js`【open_file†L296-L296】)\n\n3. **Run‑artifact shows the test wrote a `.env` file, not `.env.gates`**, and the script still printed `Env: PAPER` because `LIVE_TRADING` was never loaded into `process.env`.  \n   ```\n   command=bash -c echo 'LIVE_TRADING=true' > .env && node scripts/generate-live-proof.js\n   ...\n   Env: PAPER\n   ```  \n   (lines 1‑15 of `ogz-meta/cognition-history/mercury-execution/2026-09-01T00-35-38-523Z-run-generate-proof-env.log`【open_file†L1-L15】)\n\n4. **Specification confirms `.env.gates` is an intentional, local‑only side‑car used only by the proof generator**. It is **not** the regular `.env` file used by the rest of the platform.  \n   ```\n   A **local‑only secrets/config sidecar** loaded by `scripts/generate-live-proof.js` … It is **not committed to git** …\n   ```  \n   (lines 17‑20 of `ogz-meta/specs/phase1-env-gates-investigation.md`【open_file†L17-L20】)\n\n5. **The spec lists the only consumer of `.env.gates` as the proof generator** and notes that live PM2 processes do **not** load it.  \n   ```\n   | Direct dotenv load | `scripts/generate-live‑proof.js:277` | Always when script runs … |\n   | Indirect via DOTENV_CONFIG_PATH | `foundation/ConfigLoader.js:100` … | Only when process env has `DOTENV_CONFIG_PATH=.env.gates` |\n   ```  \n   (lines 35‑41 of `ogz-meta/specs/phase1-env-gates-investigation.md`【open_file†L35-L41】)\n\n*Conclusion*\n\nThe observed “Env: PAPER” result is expected when the script is invoked after only a `.env` file, because the script deliberately reads `.env.gates`. The `.env.gates` file is a purposeful, git‑ignored side‑car for the proof generator, and the platform’s normal `.env` is unrelated to this script. Therefore there is **no concrete break** in the current code. The original claim is a misunderstanding of the intended environment‑file usage.","tool_calls":[],"tool_call_id":null},"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":15403,"completion_tokens":765,"total_tokens":16168,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":4751},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":142}},"warning":null,"reasoning_summary":null}